      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Subject: {{$json[\"subject\"]}}\n\nBody:\n{{$json[\"textPlain\"] ?? $json[\"textHtml\"] ?? $json[\"snippet\"] ?? \"\"}}",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "You are an email classifier for IDW support.\n\nGiven the email subject and body, you must:\n1. Classify the email into exactly ONE of the following categories:\n   - \"MisssingData\"\n   - \"IncorrectData\"\n   - \"Delay\"\n\n2. Based on the chosen category, extract attributes and return a single JSON object with keys \"category\" and \"attributes\".\n\nFor each category, extract these attributes:\n- If category = \"MisssingData\":\n    attributes must contain:\n      - \"Indexmarker\" (string or null)\n      - \"Type_of_data\" (array of strings indicating what data is missing)\n      - \"shipment_date\" (always null for this category)\n\n- If category = \"IncorrectData\":\n    attributes must contain:\n      - \"Indexmarker\" (string or null)\n      - \"Type_of_data\" (array of strings indicating what data is incorrect)\n      - \"shipment_date\" (always null for this category)\n\n- If category = \"Delay\":\n    attributes must contain:\n      - \"Indexmarker\" (string or null)\n      - \"shipment_date\" (string date if mentioned, otherwise null)\n      - \"Type_of_data\" (array of strings indicating what data is delayed)\n\n3. If any attribute is not explicitly present in the email, set it to null or an empty array as appropriate.\n\n4. Your response MUST be ONLY a single JSON object, for example:\n{\n  \"category\": \"MisssingData\",\n  \"attributes\": {\n    \"Indexmarker\": \"RU5000\",\n    \"Type_of_data\": [\"T1\", \"T2\", \"T3\", \"T4\", \"T5\"],\n    \"shipment_date\": null\n  }\n}\n\nDo not include any explanatory text or additional fields outside this JSON object."
        }
      },
